# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Kill switches (incident response)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by: src/lib/resilience/kill-switches.ts
# One switch per subsystem, each with a degraded path that is not an error page.
# Strict truthiness: only 1 / true / on / yes turn a switch ON. Unset, empty,
# malformed or differently-cased all mean OFF, because a kill switch that engages
# by accident takes a working subsystem out of the shop.
#
# HOW FAST THEY TAKE EFFECT. The values are read at CALL time, not at module
# load, so a serverless instance honours a change as soon as it is given one --
# which on Vercel still means the next instance, not the one currently serving
# the request that woke you. A truly deploy-free switch needs a table, and that
# table does not exist yet. Know which one you have before an incident.

# [optional] Skip the cache layer and read straight from Postgres. Slower, never
# wrong: everything cached is derived from the database.
# KILL_SWITCH_CACHE=

# [optional] Search answers an empty result set instead of an error. A search box
# returning nothing is a degraded shop; one that 500s is a broken one.
# KILL_SWITCH_SEARCH=

# [optional] Recommendation strips render nothing rather than erroring the page.
# KILL_SWITCH_RECS=

# [optional] Suppress outbound notifications (email, push). The event is still
# recorded; only the send is skipped, so nothing is lost that cannot be resent.
# KILL_SWITCH_NOTIFICATIONS=


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI agents (off by default, and off is the safe state)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by: src/server/ai/client.ts
# TWO GATES, BOTH REQUIRED. `AI_AGENTS_ENABLED` must be plainly true AND the
# per-agent flag must be, or the call refuses before any network. Same strict
# truthiness as the kill switches, inverted: an agent that is on by accident
# spends money and talks to customers.
#
# Agents advise and never write. Nothing in that module touches the database
# beyond the `ai_usage` row that counts tokens and cost; a suggested product
# change becomes a DRAFT for an admin. The pricing agent may never touch
# platform_percent.

# [optional] The master gate. Fallback when unset: every agent refuses.
# AI_AGENTS_ENABLED=false

# [optional] Per-agent gates. Each needs the master gate as well.
# AI_AGENT_PRODUCT_DESCRIPTION=false
# AI_AGENT_SUPPORT_CHAT=false
# AI_AGENT_PRICING_ADVISOR=false
# AI_AGENT_FRAUD_SIGNALS=false

# [optional] Source: console.anthropic.com > API keys. Without it every agent
# call returns { ok: false, reason: 'no_api_key' } instead of throwing.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [platform] Injected. Do not set by hand.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NODE_ENV                          set by Next and by the test runner. Note that
#                                   `next start` on a laptop is ALSO production.
# NEXT_RUNTIME                      set by Next; src/instrumentation.ts branches on it
# VERCEL_URL                        per-deployment host, injected by Vercel
# VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA             injected by Vercel; the Sentry release fallback
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA injected by Vercel; read by instrumentation-client.ts
# CI                                set by the CI runner; makes Playwright fail on
#                                   .only and retry twice


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [optional] Local escape hatch
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by: src/lib/env.ts
# Set to "true" to let a NODE_ENV=production boot proceed without the Cardcom
# and Supabase secrets. This is what makes `pnpm start` on a laptop work for the
# Playwright suite and the Lighthouse runs, which must measure the real build.
# Without it those boots answer 500 on every route with
# "An error occurred while loading instrumentation hook".
# It logs a warning at boot every time. Vercel must never set it.
# ALLOW_INCOMPLETE_ENV=true


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Infrastructure cost pull (admin > costs)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# All four are [optional] and ALL FOUR ARE UNSET, measured 2026-09-09. Read
# indirectly by src/lib/costs/providers.ts (providerAvailability), which reads
# process.env by the name recorded against each provider, so a grep for
# `process.env.VERCEL_API_TOKEN` finds nothing and the variable is read anyway.
#
# MANUAL ENTRY IS THE WORKING PATH, NOT THE FALLBACK. With none of these set,
# every provider reports `manual` and the admin screen asks for the number.
# Setting one does not switch anything on by itself -- no client is written yet;
# it makes `providerAvailability` stop naming that provider as blocked. The
# endpoint each one would call is in providers.ts.

# Source: Vercel > Account Settings > Tokens.
# The team and project ids would still need supplying separately: the CLI here
# is installed and unauthenticated.
# VERCEL_API_TOKEN=

# Source: https://supabase.com/dashboard/account/tokens (account level).
# NOT the service role key, which is scoped to the database and cannot see an
# invoice. Same kind of token as SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN in the tooling block.
# SUPABASE_MANAGEMENT_TOKEN=

# Source: Upstash console > Account > Management API.
# NOT UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN, which IS set in this project and grants access
# to the DATABASE rather than to the account. A pull written against it 401s
# forever, and the natural conclusion would be that the value was wrong rather
# than that it was the wrong kind of credential.
# UPSTASH_MANAGEMENT_API_KEY=

# Source: Cloudflare dashboard > My Profile > API Tokens.
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=


# =============================================================================
# [tooling] Scripts, tests and CI. Never set any of these in Vercel.
# =============================================================================

# --- Database access for scripts -------------------------------------------
# Source: Supabase > Project Settings > Database > connection string.
# DATABASE_URL=            # scripts/check-rls.mjs
# SUPABASE_DB_URL=         # scripts/db-doc.mjs, scripts/_voucher-race.mjs
# SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=            # scripts/security-probe-views.mjs
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY= # same script, the public-prefixed alias

# --- Disaster recovery (scripts/dr/) ----------------------------------------
# The procedures these belong to are in docs/BACKUP-RECOVERY.md.
#
# KE_ENV_BACKUP_PASSPHRASE=  # REQUIRED by env-backup.mjs and env-restore.mjs;
#                          # both refuse without it, and the backup refuses a
#                          # passphrase under 12 characters. AES-256-CBC over
#                          # PBKDF2. Keep it in the password manager, NOT here
#                          # and not in the backup it protects.
# KE_ENV_BACKUP_DIR=       # where the encrypted bundle lands. Default
#                          # ~/ke-secrets. Writing anywhere inside the git
#                          # working tree is refused outright.
# SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=   # scripts/dr/pitr-status.mjs. A personal access
#                          # token (sbp_...) from
#                          # https://supabase.com/dashboard/account/tokens.
#                          # NOT the service or anon key: this is the
#                          # account-level API and the project keys have no
#                          # access to it. Read-only is enough. Unset, the
#                          # check exits `cannot measure` rather than guessing.
# SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF=    # same script. Default ixvwfbuvfxxsjiywhbbb, this
#                          # project. Only set it to ask about another one.

# --- E2E suite (e2e/, scripts/seed-test-data.mjs) ---------------------------
# Accounts the Playwright suite signs in as. Created by seed-test-data.mjs.
# E2E_CUSTOMER_EMAIL=
# E2E_CUSTOMER_PASSWORD=
# E2E_SUPPLIER_EMAIL=
# E2E_SUPPLIER_PASSWORD=
# E2E_ADMIN_EMAIL=         # default e2e-admin@test.kenyonexpress.local
# E2E_ADMIN_PASSWORD=      # the admin-refund spec signs in as this account
# E2E_PAID_FLOW=           # set to run the specs that require a real paid order
#
# The seed refuses to run against the production project (scripts/seed-target-guard.mjs).
# SEED_ALLOW_PRODUCTION=   # the ONLY accepted value is `i-understand`, and it
#                          # disarms that refusal. seed-test-data.mjs writes auth
#                          # users whose passwords are published in this repo, so
#                          # setting this against production creates an admin
#                          # backdoor. There is no legitimate reason to set it.
#
# How the suite is pointed at a server. All five read by playwright.config.ts.
# E2E_BASE_URL=            # point the suite at an ALREADY-RUNNING server. Setting
#                          # it makes Playwright start no server, so its own env
#                          # block (CARDCOM_USE_MOCK, CARDCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET,
#                          # CHECKOUT_ENABLED) is NOT applied and the paid-flow
#                          # specs fail for environmental reasons unless you pass
#                          # those to the server yourself.
# E2E_PORT=                # default 3000. Set it in a parallel worktree so two
#                          # checkouts do not fight over the same port.
# E2E_WEB_COMMAND=         # default `pnpm dev`. CI sets `pnpm start`, and so
#                          # should you: a bare run reuses a stale dev server and
#                          # fabricates cart failures that a real build does not have.
# E2E_WORKERS=             # default 2 locally, forced to 1 when CI is set.
# VERCEL_AUTOMATION_BYPASS_SECRET=  # sent as x-vercel-protection-bypass so the
#                          # suite can reach a deployment behind Vercel's
#                          # protection. Source: Vercel > Project Settings >
#                          # Deployment Protection > Protection Bypass for Automation.
# DEV_ADMIN_EMAIL=         # scripts/_admin-shot.mjs
# DEV_ADMIN_PASSWORD=      # scripts/_admin-shot.mjs

