# Source: WordPress > WooCommerce > Settings > Advanced > REST API.
# WC_BASE=https://kenyonexpress.co.il
# WC_KEY=
# WC_SECRET=
# WP_IMPORT_ALLOW_WRITES=  # the importer is read-only until this is set

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Twilio WhatsApp (order-status notifications + inbound support webhook)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [optional] Read by: src/server/whatsapp/twilio.ts
# Source: Twilio Console > Account Info. All three or the feature is off:
# outbound sends report `skipped` and the inbound webhook answers 401.
# TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
# TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
# TWILIO_WHATSAPP_FROM=+14155238886

# [optional] Read by: src/app/api/webhooks/whatsapp/route.ts
# Source: the exact URL configured in Twilio Console > WhatsApp Sandbox /
# Sender > "When a message comes in". Twilio signs that string, so a proxy
# that rewrites the host breaks validation unless this names the original.
# Fallback when unset: NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL + /api/webhooks/whatsapp.
# TWILIO_WEBHOOK_URL=

# [optional] Read by: src/lib/whatsapp/outbox.ts (buildWhatsappMessage)
# Source: Twilio Console > Content Template Builder, after WhatsApp approval.
# One SID per queued message kind. WITHOUT THE SID THAT KIND IS SILENTLY NOT
# SENT: buildWhatsappMessage returns null and the outbox row is skipped, which
# is the approval blocker showing through rather than a bug. Each template takes
# three positional variables: {{1}} voucher code, {{2}} business name,
# {{3}} expiry date in Hebrew.
# TWILIO_CONTENT_SID_VOUCHER_ISSUED=
# TWILIO_CONTENT_SID_VOUCHER_EXPIRING=
